The public halves of the keys EveSynapse releases are signed with.

`evesynapse -update` installs a release only when its manifest is
signed by a key listed here, and the release job refuses to sign with
a key that is not. One PEM block per key; everything outside the
blocks, like this text, is commentary.

A key can carry a name for the updater to report its signer by: a
"Label:" line in the commentary directly above the key's block, its
text the name. A key with no such line is reported by its
fingerprint alone.

A key is added by the tool that makes it, which writes the private
half to a file for the release job's CI/CD variable and never
shows it:

    go run ./cmd/releasesign keygen -out ~/evesynapse-release-key.pem

"Release signing" in the README covers replacing a key and what to do
if one is lost. Only public keys belong in this file.

-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEARnB9SqpA6cDuYQkHBA4zFu0KvWhDP85WmcN5kKxPiWI=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----

Label: nate@evesynapse.app / natemsz
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MCowBQYDK2VwAyEAmaFCxLtA1O3HxV8OTGGug+jPhpb+9x87SCdU+thQAmc=
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
